## Install

```sh
npm install
cargo check --workspace        # verify the Rust workspace compiles
```

<% if (variant === "standalone") { %>## Run

Start the bundled sample widget and the Terminal in separate shells:

```sh
npm run dev:sample-widget      # http://localhost:3012
npm run dev:terminal           # opens the Terminal window
```

The Terminal reads the widget catalog from [`widgets.config.json`](./widgets.config.json) at the workspace root — edit that file (or use `npm run create-widget`) to add more widgets.

## Connect to an FDC3 agent

This Standalone workspace acts as an **FDC3 client**. Point it at an external FDC3 agent by setting `fdc3.agentUrl` in [`apps/one-terminal/src-tauri/resources/terminal.config.json`](./apps/one-terminal/src-tauri/resources/terminal.config.json):

```json
{
  "fdc3": { "agentUrl": "ws://your-agent.example.com:7891/fdc3" }
}
```

Leave it empty if you don't have an agent yet — widgets that call `getAgent()` will get a clear `NoAgentConfigured` rejection instead of silently hanging.

<% } else { %>## Run

Start the three services in separate shells:

```sh
npm run dev:app-directory      # http://localhost:<%= appDirectoryPort %>
npm run dev:desktop-agent      # FDC3 broker + engine launcher
npm run dev:terminal           # opens the Terminal window
```

The App Directory ships with two demo apps (`sample-ticker` on port 3010, `sample-chart` on port 3011). Edit [`apps/app-directory/src/data.ts`](./apps/app-directory/src/data.ts) to add your own apps, or use the management UI at `http://localhost:<%= appDirectoryPort %>`.

<% } %>## Add a widget

```sh
npm run create-widget                                                       # interactive
npm run create-widget -- --name fx-rates --title "FX Rates" --port 3010     # scripted
```

[`scripts/new-widget.mjs`](./scripts/new-widget.mjs) is a zero-dependency Node script (standard library only — works offline). Edit [`scripts/widget-template/`](./scripts/widget-template/) to customise the boilerplate new widgets are built from.<% if (variant === "standalone") { %> New widgets are auto-registered in `widgets.config.json`.<% } else { %> The script prints a `curl POST /v2/apps` command for the App Directory, or registers automatically if `OT_APPD_TOKEN` and `OT_APP_DIR_URL` are set.<% } %>

